112301,9qJyDlZst8c,UgwaqNObSJpnVNYnp2Z4AaABAg,2020-07-25T09:07:35Z,1,0,"Spoiler Below, just for the oddballs that want to know the backstory. I mean, like a really really really big spoiler, you probaly don't even have to read the light novel after this.















Almost there...


















Shin, Anos's subordinate was the one who actually started spreading the rumour about The Demon King of Tyranny being Avos Dilhevia. He did that in order to protect Anos and his daughter Misa Iriologue, who should appear around chapter 5-6 probably. Her mother, as the LN explains, is a Great Spirit, which also explains her powerful abilities. So the whole ordeal of Anos's name being forgotten was nothing more than his subordinate's Shin intent to protect his daughter Misa (as she was meant to revive/be born after 2000 years, just like Anos) and Anos's identity.

Basically a misunderstanding on Anos's part.

By the way, if you consider the relationship between Anos and Shin, Misa could probably call Anos his uncle or something.

Oh, and another little thing... 
Misa is actually Avos Dilhevia, as she is a spirit, something fictional, she was actually birthed from the concept of Avos that people had.

Hope you have a nice day."
