171627,tAzAhDNdehs,UgxZYemgak6soAfSN9V4AaABAg,2025-07-04T03:31:00Z,2,0,"As long as the director understands the point of color in Chainsaw Man, the style change will be good.

Any proper criticism of the style for Season 1 has to be about how the color was made a less important aspect of the storytelling, which can be considered a flaw. Even as a staunch enjoyer of Ryuu Nakayama's approach, some precise color choices would have been welcome.

I hope this approach utilizes color in the way the manga did, not as an aesthetic, but as a storytelling tool. This is not DanDaDan, which is also phenomenal, but not the same, and those who think this should have the color of that, misunderstood the meaning of color in Chainsaw Man.

This trailer gives me some hope that I didn't have before, I think it might be just a bit too far on the colorful side, but I can't fault the director for overstepping in his own way just as Nakayama did. Even so, there are several moments shown so far that really do feel like Chainsaw Man's color was understood well.

Regardless, I'm excited, just a bit hesitant is all."
