124153,guStf5P4Js0,UgwWOKVXUiwe2dDVlil4AaABAg,2024-01-29T01:56:47Z,0,0,i do also wish sk8 had leaned more into the subcultures and stuff that it briefly seemed to go over and like. more about yk. skateboarding. like there certainly was some of that but like it’d definitely help develop its themes to go over it more
124153,guStf5P4Js0,Ugx0DFyAWggVtWSicHp4AaABAg,2024-01-28T21:36:21Z,0,0,i do enjoy this show a lot for what it is - i think the fact that a lot of the marketing centers on the selling of some of the character’s perceived attractiveness is in part its own downfall in getting the narrative of the story really right (i feel like this also goes for many other stories out there though) because it was and did go really interesting places!!! but the fact that a lot of this theme was shown through a character who’s mixed ideas ended up hitting badly even if they had an interesting foundation going in is just. eeeeeeeeehhhhhh. in general the stuff going on with all of the adult characters in different ways and the repression of personal self-expression into a secret identity of sorts while living in a capitalist society is like. this hits!!! it’s an incredibly queer narrative and it makes me wish that everything with adam had been handled better because he’s super interesting as a character but the added factor of the queer villain stereotype (which really isn’t terrible if done well - villains and antagonists are fun when campy! but why do flamboyant queer characters always need to be villainous??) and the fact that he’s incredibly weird to a 17 year old for most of the show really does feel kind of insidious and definitely hinges on some deeply homophobic ideas. just. eeeuhhhh. i am excited for the OVAs and s2 but i hope they can do better regarding this - i still do enjoy watching the show so ik there’ll be stuff i like no matter what but!
