153518,n5JEoD7keVo,UgwE2z3ICopnOpxwlAF4AaABAg,2023-12-21T03:41:01Z,0,0,"Hello from Japan🇯🇵🇯🇵🇯🇵
Trailer sees giant carp, scorpions and octopuses.
If we had such giant-sized ingredients, we could make lots of different kinds of food.
Such a trip would probably be great fun.
They may need to picture several thick cookbooks of recipes in their head.
From a Japanese point of view, the shape and flesh of scorpions are similar to the image of crustaceans such as prawns and crabs, so I think they could probably be used as a very good soup stock for a variety of dishes.
Oh, it would smell as good as Gyokai ramen (ramen made with seafood broth) at a ramen shop...
It looks like it could be used in soup with a large amount of vegetables.
I also think it could be cooked with meat, or mixed with rice to make risotto.
I am sure it would be delicious in this anime.
In the real world, it is impossible to actually eat scorpions because they are highly poisonous, and I don't want to eat them.
But how would they make it non-toxic?
Would it be the same procedure as when you detoxify pufferfish poison in the real world?
But then I would have to go to school to become a professional chef, and I would have to get a qualification... How would I handle it in this world in this animation?
It's quite interesting."
