153518,U3veqJewdto,UgwmihgCVwRId6B8xpt4AaABAg,2023-10-02T03:17:28Z,1,0,"Not to spoil anything, but it's kind of funny how much more serious this series gets after a while compared to the quirky ""monster to cook of the week"" plot it had in the beginning. :p I'm not really sure how to feel about that, I loved the creativity it had in the beginning. :? I guess the rest of the story has it's own interesting lore and drama to tell too, but yeah. :p

Anyways, the entire manga is already finished and can be read on places like Manganato if you people don't already know. :p I didn't think it would take so long to get animated though. :? This seems like the type of quirky new age thing that would have already been done a long time ago. :p"
153518,U3veqJewdto,Ugw1W45lcGTx7UrnSP14AaABAg,2023-09-27T10:34:46Z,0,0,YOOOO
153518,U3veqJewdto,Ugwv6neTIhm4i3f_RO14AaABAg,2023-09-26T17:37:27Z,16,0,"Imo the fantasy manga with the best world building I've ever read. The dungeon ecosystem is very detailed and impressive, not to mention the care put in all the fantasy races and different cultures. All the characters were distinctive and likeable, even someone I thought would be the antagonist at first would turn out to be a nice person, just with different view from our main characters.
The plot was simple and straight-forward, but in a way this was also Dungeon Meshi's charming point. I'm so glad it have finished now with a marvelous ending, can't wait for the anime!!"
