153518,U3veqJewdto,UgwJsLjuPrxlQP5ZwfB4AaABAg,2023-08-17T19:29:32Z,27,0,"Ah, when it starts out as a fun Food-focused series, then it becomes one of the best well written and amazing world-building stories near the end.   The author's ideas in creating the ecosystem of the Dungeon is amazing.
SPOILERS:

Favorite one is probably how treasure bugs and mimic-chests are done.   Mimics in this world are basically Hermit-Crabs of varying sizes.   Biggest one looks like a Coconut-Crab that uses a chest (or any portable storage) as it's Shell.
Treasure bugs, as the name suggests, bugs that resemble treasure and coins.   To eat and reproduce, they act like parasitic bugs to Mimics.  They enter a Mimic-Chest, lay eggs.  Then the larvae hatches and eats the Mimics from the inside.  Replacing the contents of the chest with more Treasure-Bugs.   To spread, Adventurer's would fine these ""hollowed"" out chests and carry home ""treasure"" thinking they'll be rich.  Only for the coins to suddenly sprout bug wings to attack them or fly away to look for more mimics."
