108489,M0CsMI-qqmI,Ugz9co7pHFV4CairrMJ4AaABAg,2020-07-11T03:35:38Z,0,1,"1st episode of season 3 was great: SPOILERS BELOW

1. It started off with some closure to the last episode of season 2's cliffhanger where Yukinon reveals more of herself to Hachiman and Yui - there is also reminiscence flashbacks to their times together in season 1 & 2, specifically season 1 where it all started out and Yukinon helped Yui bake cookies for Hachiman (I think it's the service club's first task and the first time they spend hanging out with each other)
2. Then we get some bro-sis time with sis-con Hachiman and his little sister Komachi who tells him how grateful she is to him for always being there for her no matter when and that this will always be true no matter what her results are for her highschool entrance exams - at this point 8man Hachiman tears up thinking that Komachi is becoming all grown up now... wwaaaahhh!!! They share a touching emotional moment together (I'm crying too Hachiman, I don't wanna let her go and see her get married off to another man!)
3. Finally we get some cute interaction between Kawasaki-san (grey hair) and her little sister with Hachiman and Komachi to close episode 1 of the season off :). Kawasaki-san's little sis calls Hachiman by the nickname ""Haa-chan"" which I thought is pretty funny and Hachiman responds by telling her to be wary of other men and that they might get the wrong idea by her being all touchy-feely (LOL I was like seriously...) - then Kawasaki shoots back at him by questioning what things 8man's teaching her little sister. Then Hachiman and Kawasaki talk in the cafe for a bit - we get a flashback to season 1 with Hachiman and Kawasaki at the festival where she goes all TSUNDERE behind the scenes after interacting with Hachiman (I was like LOL are we getting another addition to the HAREM? haha) - Komachi then comes into the cafe with them and says she's thirsty and Hachiman hands her his cup of water to which she replies ""Gross"" and they have some friendly bro-sis banter..."
