108489,M0CsMI-qqmI,UgzTs_pIDUtqngfpl594AaABAg,2020-07-09T05:42:29Z,1,0,"I started SNAFU about two months ago, maybe it was around May and now I am close to finishing up SNAFU TOO. During this time, I lost passion for anime and lost interest in new seasonal ones aside from sequels that I have long committed to and the ones on my to watchlist. Two days ago I realized I had also developed an odd case of Nostalgia Syndrome during the pandemic when a lot of anime were delayed like this one which gave me time to watch SNAFU.
I try to watch an episode or so of SNAFU every night and now I am almost finished with SNAFU TOO. All so I can reach to this point. Because I have come to realize, my passion for this series though hard to accept for drama genre anime is my greatest bane, was genuine and I am happy I have started and committed to it. More importantly, I cannot wait to see how this story will come to a close. 
What I have realized during 2020 with my Nostalgia Syndrome and loss of passion for anime, is that unless you jump out of the bandwagon of top anime every season, you will never know which anime that are true precious marvels. 
I jumped out of the bandwagon, stopped watching seasonal anime, and here I am."
