113717,fXmAurh012s,UgxEZVOIk3YtYSGQOFR4AaABAg,2023-11-25T00:42:47Z,330,18,"My 18 year old daughter asked me to watch this show on Thanksgiving Day with her. I am 47, and fighting Stage IV Breast, Bone, Spine, Incurrable Cancer. We stayed up until 7am, crying, screaming, yelling, laughing. We are a Military Family. The creator, who fought for this show to begin and end. Wow. My daughter told me to watch the documentary, and I will. This show made me think about my own issues with my older sister. This show is magical. The face expressions, the emotions of these characters, BRAVO. I salute the individual who was told that this show was not going to make it. Never give up on your dreams I keep telling my 4 kids. I am finishing my BA online for this reason. You have to keep pushing, when someone says, you can't? Show them that YOU WILL. 

I SALUTE! The man who kept going to make this show happen. I stand up and salute you! 

I CANNOT wait...for season 2. You can't go wrong, the characters are too magical. And that will never change now. Omg, I just cannot wait! 🎉❤🎉"
