181444,1FcVJxxPWh4,UgysGIKetU0bJG0BhCR4AaABAg,2026-02-01T15:49:42Z,4,2,"People say this anime is a breath of fresh air for its positivity and cute, light-hearted aesthetic. I think this is taken to extremes in the anime. I'm sorry, but those can't be the real problems, because REAL PEOPLE aren't like that. There are no two-dimensional, always-smiling, forgiving girls. There are no ""gentle giants""—perfect, cute, and sweet guys. People don't get emotional and blush over every FUCKING INTERACTION. The problems it tries to address are real, but they're approached in a totally unrealistic way, meant to please the naive viewer who believes in those standards and that way of relating to people. Positive masculinity is certainly a great thing, and while the relationships between male friends are my favorite thing about the anime, I can't help but notice how there's never any room for REAL conflict here either. For REAL arguments, disagreements, and complexities.  All of this results in an overly sappy, repetitive experience, a huge fetish for shyness. It's immature just because it talks about emotions without a drop of toxicity. It's the same old corporate bullshit."
