181444,1FcVJxxPWh4,UgzPQY6V1PpDPeTYTNp4AaABAg,2026-01-30T03:32:20Z,2,1,"Anybody who's on the fence about watching this, allow me to give it a glowing review. I spent 5 years studying literature at an academic level. This show hits more emotional beats and has more character growth than nearly anything else that runs only 12-13 episodes. And the manga goes even deeper. The show itself does begin to feel a little streamlined and rushed, but it has a satisfying ending and IT addresses real life emotional issues such as overcoming self-esteem and doubt in a realistic and fulfilling way.

This is not a generic heroic character with dead parents either. The protagonist has a healthy relationship with both his mother and his father, including scenes of real mentorship with his father. These family Dynamics are so important for people who are sorely lacking them in the Modern Age. I almost never say this because my academic education has conditioned me to have high standards, but this is a real work of art and there's very little that's so directly addresses real life needs such as emotional such as emotional maturity and human interconnectivity.

One of the longest psychological studies ever done searched for what was the one common factor that made people happiest and most joyful over the long run. This intergenerational study found that it was human connection, and this show illustrates people struggling and eventually achieving connections, not just romantically but also through friendships. Not in an easy straightforward way, but through overcoming trauma and issues with a low self esteem.

The world needs a hundred more shows like this, but for now I encourage you to start with this one."
