181444,1FcVJxxPWh4,Ugz8PIbIEXxX26GxdZR4AaABAg,2025-11-28T18:23:09Z,0,0,"The first 2 episodes are cute but then you start to notice it's just an apology simulator. 

""I'm sorry for making you feel that way"", ""I'm sorry for putting you in danger"" (there was no danger), ""I'm sorry for my prejudice"" etc...; constantly apologizing for the most minimal offenses. It tries way too hard to be an emotional feel good story while lacking any real depth or stakes; and at the same time, acting as if the offenses are the end of the world. 

If you're emotionally sensitive to these sorts of things then you might find it interesting. I found it boring and annoying but I'm probably not the target audience. I just can't stand when people apologize for being themselves, especially when they did nothing wrong. But, I understand that some people may experience anxiety and often irrationally feel like a burden to others. Those who can relate to this sentiment may enjoy this anime."
