181444,1FcVJxxPWh4,Ugw7ljDKdIlu25INh2B4AaABAg,2025-09-28T15:38:19Z,0,0,"The romance is SO well written and well developed. I love that part of this show.

I really struggle with the radioactively toxic negativity of the school's animosity towards one another. Like it actually really makes it very difficult to watch.

I mean, it seems to be a central part of the show so far... so its not like an accident or poor design decision ... its difficult on purpose to make a point. It seems to serve as a backdrop to provide context for what I assume will be character development as they wrestle with it and begin to ask deeper questions and grow as people in pursuit of the answers to those questions.

So I write the above to clarify that I'm not bashing the show or failing to see its' good points. 

But it still makes it really hard to keep watching despite the FANTASTIC romance. I think i'll keep going thru it each week. Its written well enough that I feel like I just gotta have a little faith and keep giving it a chance."
