181444,X5NzgNM_VAc,UgxiDG-3NLK3DAlP0Z54AaABAg,2025-11-16T02:07:16Z,0,0,"Let me write calculus:For those who don't know: differentiation is the process where we find a derivative(a very small of a variable like x) in relation to the variable. To differentiate (also known as to take the derivation) we substract the power(n) with 1. Then we multiply the power with the variable. This is nothing but nx^n-1. It is indicated by alphabet d. Integration is nothing but anti differentiation. Here we add up all thetiny bits (derivatives). There are two types, indefinite defenite integrals. We simply add one power to the variable and also take the same power and add and put it below the variable(fraction). Then we +c if indefenite integral or switch the variable with upper limit and power limit and substract them. It's in the form of x^n+1/n+1+c. Haha"
