181444,X5NzgNM_VAc,UgzGyDRB6sYfAgc1iRd4AaABAg,2025-09-09T04:41:29Z,2,0,"I’m honestly so disappointed with the Fragrant Flower Blooms With Dignity dub. I only watch anime in dub, and I’ve waited months upon months for Blue Box—and that dub did not disappoint. But this one feels rushed and just weird. Rintaro’s VA is solid, but our dear main character sounds like someone just trying to act like a girl instead of naturally fitting the role. I would rather wait another 6 months for a proper dub than get something that feels this off. Ironically, this ended up being the first anime I watched subbed because of how much the dub let me down."
181444,X5NzgNM_VAc,UgwwihmedgoTKWqiVnd4AaABAg,2025-09-09T01:10:45Z,2,0,I couldn’t wait for the North America drop . I didn’t want to rush my Canadian summer of 8 weeks . I’m on episode 10 and I hope you all enjoy it as much as I have .
181444,X5NzgNM_VAc,UgxvsMw5EqQ5OEk4grZ4AaABAg,2025-09-09T00:31:12Z,1,0,"Y’all are so damn dramatic. The voices are fine. And to clear up the seemingly buttload of misinformation floating around online and in this comment section.

1.) She is not voiced by Aleks Le (??)
2.) She is not voiced by Casey Mongillo, either.
3.) The male lead is voiced by Robbie Daymond, an incredibly prominent anime and video game VA, so, no, they didn’t “outsource to live action actors” (??)
4.) The actual VA of the female lead is Bijou Vann, who also has some anime credits under her belt, but she’s a little newer.
5.) Bijou Vann is a woman. So they don’t need to cast “an actual woman.” Not that it should matter. I know it’s somewhat subjective, but her performance is literally fine.

Literally all of this could be avoided if you used those handy dandy little mobile devices and looked up a cast list. Or watched the credits. It shouldn’t be this hard to know who voices who in an anime."
