108430,24YrEAGF32M,Ugy05h89RSi1rejFqa14AaABAg,2019-09-23T21:11:07Z,1,0,"Where i come from relationships are frowned upon, meaning that i can't visit her place or go out for movies and stuff either. We ""went"" for drives tho, and the closest we could get was to hold hands (or awkward but glad hugs!) , Which changed a week ago when i somehow managed to bring her to my place, i was home alone and up for the risk of getting caught since i had to move 6000 miles from her for studies, all i wanted was one day. It was a fun day, she was there for a few hours and we watched this movie, i didn't know what it was about (human touch! That I'd soon be missing, her's... The only one i need). Even after 3 years of the relationship, I was still nervous to hold her hand during the movie, But i did and she put her head on my shoulder after a while, it was like breathing for the first time. The movie ended and it left her quietly sobbing on my shoulder, asking me to stay. I held her in my arms and close wasn't close enough. Talked to her to calm her down and... She did, eventually. I held her face and kissed her forehead, we then kissed for the first time, told that her that we'll be fine and make it work, she kissed me again and i won't ever forget her lips, sweeter than cherry. It gets alone in here and not an hour goes by that i don't think about her, Sometimes when I'm walking, i look up at the sky and say to my self that at least were under the same sky. Anyways, the moral really is that ""if you're able, touch him, touch her"""
