178788,x7uLutVRBfI,Ugw0p3RzgDgFXXo0kn94AaABAg,2026-08-06T13:09:54Z,1,0,"New Character Proposal – Ren Kibutsuji (Ice Hashira)

Character Name: Ren Kibutsuji (連 鬼舞辻)

Title: Ice Hashira (The Frozen Pillar)

Nature:
Ren Kibutsuji is a calm, disciplined, and silent swordsman who rarely speaks. He always puts innocent lives before his own and never lets emotions cloud his judgment. During battle, his presence feels as cold and quiet as a snowstorm, yet his determination is unbreakable.

Breathing Style

Ice Breathing (氷の呼吸 – Kōri no Kokyū)

A breathing style that focuses on speed, precision, and overwhelming cold. Every slash is accompanied by freezing winds and crystal-like ice effects that overwhelm demons with relentless attacks.

First Form – Ice Slash

A lightning-fast sword strike that releases a freezing slash capable of cutting through multiple enemies in an instant.

Second Form – Frost Tide

A continuous series of flowing attacks that spread like an icy wave, trapping demons in relentless pressure.

Third Form – Crystal Shard Lake

The battlefield becomes covered with razor-sharp ice crystals that erupt toward demons from every direction.

Fourth Form – Blizzard

Ren disappears within a violent snowstorm, moving at incredible speed while striking from unseen angles.

Fifth Form – Ice Dragon

Ren unleashes a massive dragon of ice that surges toward the enemy with overwhelming force, freezing everything in its path.

Hidden Sixth Form – Cosmic Glacial Impact

Ren's forbidden and ultimate technique.

He releases every ounce of his strength, creating a frozen domain with a radius of nearly 7 kilometers. Endless glacial energy fills the battlefield as countless microscopic ice particles rush toward every demon within range. In a single moment, demons are struck from every direction and sliced into hundreds of pieces before they can react.

This technique consumes nearly all of Ren's stamina and can only be used as a final resort, making it the most dangerous form of Ice Breathing.

Quote:
""When winter arrives... even demons learn the meaning of silence."""
