178788,x7uLutVRBfI,UgzyXEQAYhX_9jRYCu14AaABAg,2025-09-22T02:27:40Z,3,0,"Holy yap but: Just watched it in 4DX at Regal. It was absolutely amazing. The seats were corresponding with the movie, the use of water and snow machines, and everything overall about 4DX was so immersive. But besides the immersion, the movie itself was so incredible. I have been an Akaza fan since the Mugen Train movie, and this movie gave me more respect and appreciation for his character. I absolutely loved this movie's visuals, audio, and the plot. I love Akaza's backstory so much. I felt like I relate to him in various of ways. And also, his backstory just uncovers his vulnerable side, his past life, and it makes so much sense why he turned into a demon. I am so glad to be able to experience watching this movie in theaters especially on 4dx. I'm planning to rewatch it with friends as I went alone today. I manage to capture a lot of scenes (just for me to look at), but my phone died on a scene I really wanted to take towards the end of the movie (no spoilers), so I'm definitely going to capture that moment when i'm watching with my friends. Thank you to everyone involved in the creation of this movie! 9/21/2025."
