114963,aXc9DVfLTGo,UgzgkxVSWphGTY1r8ot4AaABAg,2020-11-10T06:39:00Z,0,0,"This movie should be called *_""The Romanticization of Sexual Harassment by a Girl That Worked Better as a Cat than as a Human""._* 
Spoilers ahead, although with a warning.
Like, boohoo, you had some sad things in your past, now you have the right and the justification to treat people around you like garbage EXCEPT the boy you like. Oh, and your best friend. That's literally the end of the list. But in reality she cares about one thing and one thing only, -herself- and the poor boy who has no idea what she actually is at first-- a completely obsessed girl, who realistically speaking could _never_ just turn out to be ""okay"" even after her wish has been granted: to date the boy she likes. She would still be the same deranged person, because surprise surprise, romance doesn't cure your mental health issues. 

She has absolutely NOTHING else she cares for in her life, yet she continuosly ignores the guy's boundaries, privacy, _and_ even abuses the physical advantages of being a cat! Yeah, she reaches a creepy level right off the bat. This gal never past the age of 7. I've seen depressed people, guys, I've struggled with depression and mental health problems, too; not a f*cking excuse, I assure you. 
The ONLY reason this girl cared about being a human again was because of, you guessed it, that poor boy-- who also becomes ""the bad one"" because he made her cry once, what a meanie :( and suddenly none of her actions matter (as if they ever did) because *SPOILER SPOILER* he actually liked her too. *END OF SPOILER* So all's fine and dandy, right?!

I mean, if you like this movie, well, what can I say. Just... imagine if this were a gender-bender... would it still be ""cute""? 
I will always hate two things: the glorification of twisted ""romance"", and the excuses of shitty people saying that traumas allow them to be shitty.  Oof. Please don't come at me with pitchforks, I'm just warning people like me who believed this might be a good movie."
