114963,aXc9DVfLTGo,Ugyh-UGs9uX9BG_qHqd4AaABAg,2020-08-10T12:46:48Z,0,0,"Maybe it’s just me but this was by far a very annoying movie for me:’) I hate myself for it cause everyone hypes it up so much but literally the only thing she focuses on is her crush to the point any other relationship or bond is so simplified and annoying to her- I hate people who are so narrow-minded like that, don’t get me wrong the animation was so good and there were cute moments. But she was a brat most of the movie and kept making the dumbest choices- the plot is almost like a furry wattpad fusion. The hype for this definitely made my expectations a bit higher and watching this right after “ A Silent Voice” make it seem that much more annoying too for the plot to be so simple. The classic, overused orphan-hero story where she hates everything but her puppy love for this boy cause he loves to do pottery and helps out in his family while watching her own interactions with her own family was painful till the ending credits where they FINALLY gave some justice to the parents. Idk this movie was a 5.5/10 at best for me, I understand lots of people love this so don’t come at me...I just hate how she uses her trauma from her past mom in the most dumbest ways and excuses...I did like the car island idea the most out of the entire movie, it was really creative and I was into the bar scene where the other cats discussed the balance of human life versus escapism to an different species. And that was the most “ deep” part of this movie. That 10 minute scene, I really tried to understand the comments of how this movie was so deep but it’s really an orphan-hero story at its core. The style and playfulness is similar to studio ghibili but the studio would focus on the cat island more/spirituality/mask trading information/truly philosophical ideas that aren’t discussed much in movies other than “ I hate the world 😃” 


Then again she is just a kid, just was extremely disappointed after everything I heard about it."
