114963,aXc9DVfLTGo,Ugywse_A861lVlZpNK14AaABAg,2020-07-20T04:00:56Z,0,0,"Here is what I thought of the movie:



I enjoyed it. The music was great (Yorushika's songs are always nice!) and I thought the animation was good. The storyline is solid as well.  I expected that the bulk of the film was gonna be the MC (Muge) traveling in the cat world to get her body back, but was pleasantly surprised that the setting mostly took place in the real world. The characters were okay but good enough (but again, it's a film so I didn't expect me to get too attached to characters in a span of an hour). However, I found Muge to be slightly annoying at times because her ostentatious personality felt a bit too much (but it makes sense for her to be over the top because she's using it to mask her depression). The movie made her seem like a damsel in distress and I felt that they made Muge's happiness depend too much on Hinode. I understand that she likes him and he did help her, but I wish they dived more into her thinking of the other people in her life and improving her relationship with herself. There are very cute scenes that made me giggle and emotional parts that moved me. 
It's a good and wholesome movie that's worth your time!"
