114963,aXc9DVfLTGo,Ugxi4sG86sqavJUJP3d4AaABAg,2020-07-12T03:34:11Z,1,2,"Spoiler warning(long rant warning): If you’re here for good character and development, Imma stop you right here- The main character is simply atrocious. Her first meeting with the ML was as a cat, and we proceed to see her being extremely clingy with no regards to personal space with the excuse that she ‘loves’ him. Throughout the movie, she proceed to disregard everyone who cares for her for the ML, absolutely no care for her friend and parents who were worried sick that she was gone. Her every inner thought is about ML. At no point do we see her mature even a single speck throughout her journey. I have never watched a movie with a more annoying protagonist. Her resolution as she finally becomes human is that she’ll ‘TRY to LIKE them’, her loving step-mom and dad who were looking all over for her sick with worry. The movie makes it seem as if she was tortured for years, except it was only her biological mom who was an ass and that she’s dealing with her parents divorce (which we see no expansion on). Saying she has depression is also a stretch considering nothing she thinks of relates to it. As she runs away from home and cries outside, her only thought is wanting ML to love her. She somewhat realizes her ungratefulness at the end, but again, her resolution was to ‘try to like them’, which makes no sense to me. Regardless of her possible mental health problems, she was a stalker who invaded ML’s personal space and hurt her friends/family with maybe a small speck of remorse. Mental health issues does not excuse this. I don’t understand how she was at all likeable, perhaps her wanting to escape is relatable, but her clingy/obsessive personality only makes her seem like an ungrateful brat. This plot could have had so much potential had the protagonist not been so shallow and self-centred. The only person she served was herself, and it’s even a stretch to say she helped ML feel better as a cat since she was doing it for her own interest (aka, stalking him)"
