114963,aXc9DVfLTGo,UgzwAqql1eJIzwXAOkt4AaABAg,2020-07-07T02:26:16Z,0,0,"I do love this movie. I'm usually not a big fan of the idea for stalking someone you love but there are a few reasons that made me able to look past it. Not make it okay, just enough to suspend my disbelief. 1. She was incredibly hurt and lonely. That of course never makes it okay but it explains why she put all her love into one boy. I see it less as creepy obsession lust after one person and more a desperate attempt to feel lovable and the ability to provide that care that a loved one could provide. 2. She's a cat. That's not something that usually comes up in these situations. 3. The concept for this movie was probably taken from the sole idea 'Wouldn't it be cool to escape my life and live as my crush's pet!' Which just reminds me that a movie doesn't have to support real world ideologies and can be used to explore a concept and be entertaining at the same time.

Then again I'm really just talking out of my ass because I liked the movie and don't want to feel guilty about it. Highly recommend."
