114963,aXc9DVfLTGo,UgwMgSCk9-Gj4gtzXtV4AaABAg,2020-06-28T01:51:15Z,43,7,"Just watched this movie, and I want to have a discussion about something... SPOILERS BELOW



*—————————SPOILER ALERT—————————*


Ok, so when she goes to Cat Island, she meets the past humans that have turned into cats. One of the female cats describes why she ran away from her problems... she says that she thought she was an inadequate mother, so she left. That sounds an awful lot like what Muge’s mother did. She “abandoned her” in grade school and then suddenly reappeared years later (after having adjusted to human life?). What if that cat was actually her mother, and another cat was living as her human mom. I was sort of expecting that this would be the case, and that Muge could get some closure (?) and reasoning behind her mother’s sudden disappearance. But now that I think about it, she would have to constantly live with the fact that her mother is stuck as a cat on Cat Island. It also doesn’t really fit with the message of the story (learning to open your heart and love everybody again). However, part of me wonders if the topic of her previous identity just never crossed their minds. And that, in reality, that cat is Muge’s mother who will live the remaining years of her shortened lifespan regretting the fact that she is no longer able to be with her family... pretty dark isn’t it..."
