105228,ZB1ACrzVDRM,Ugzba6N0z89dtIikgFp4AaABAg,2019-12-19T10:14:16Z,5,2,"I seriously have to admit, I'm incredibly disappointed by how jarringly clunky the animation style looks. Not to sound like I'm being overly nostalgic or reminiscing here, but I honestly sometimes wish animation would go back to the time when animators didn't feel like (or have the luxury of) drawing over CG models in almost EVERY FUCKING FRAME. When you use shortcuts like this so ungracefully, the nuance of the art is just, well, gone."
105228,ZB1ACrzVDRM,Ugzw2qmLglh8rq6tmyd4AaABAg,2019-12-19T06:51:57Z,1,0,The trailer looks pretty good. The CG itself looks pretty good overall but the color pallet they are using is a bit brighter than I would expect for the story. The coloration used on the manga covers is generally darker version of the colors they are using where Caiman is a dark forest green. Its just a critique nothing deal breaking though. Another detail that sticks out to me is Nikaido's face appears rounder in the anime than it does in the manga. I think that might be due to them bringing on some of the people who worked on Akira if I remember correctly. Really looking forward to the show and its insanity.
