111762,_nVe995f9HQ,UgzvPOH3xSNYFmkOX6h4AaABAg,2020-06-24T09:38:48Z,0,0,"i really wanted to like this story. i don’t know if it was the timing of when i decided to watch it, but i just feel this huge disconnect with the show and i don’t know why. maybe it’s because the story feels like it’s all over the place. i feel like every important aspect of the story is stretched so far from each other. one episode tries to introduce an important detail, but it doesn’t pick up until 3-4 episodes later. it kind of feels dreadful to be honest. by the end, i completely forgot that the first episode already hinted at kyo’s significance, simply because the gap from episode 1 to episode 23/24 barely indicated anything about him. but maybe it’s also because of tohru. her personality is a pet peeve of mine. no matter what show, what genre, what form of media, i absolutely cannot stand characters who just keep on crying about everything. granted that she is “strong”, but i just cannot stand all the crying before she actually does something. in some really intimate scenes, she just starts to act clumsy, and it breaks the atmosphere imo. i wish she would be more serious sometimes; rather, i wish her seriousness would last a bit longer than how it’s portrayed for the most part. to be honest, i don’t even know how i survived watching 25 episodes. i would’ve dropped it in episode 5, if only kyo wasn’t such an interesting and lovable character, despite him feeling so insignificant before the end."
