128705,IV0-SYn3YuM,Ugz6V-adT7UyN-uM6zt4AaABAg,2021-10-14T19:14:54Z,0,0,"I love more grounded anime like this that focus on real world settings and situations. 

After watching the first episode, the show really resonated with me. I an artists who draws off and on and I think the show is a needed reassurance that this is something I am passionate about and is something that makes me feel alive. I felt seen. There were some hard truths and lessons such as hammering in the constant amount of hard work and tenacity of following through. It is so easy to stop and take long breaks. There is a lot of mental effort that goes into art and a ton of studying. It can get very overwhelming and I think a lot of artists like myself lean towards being perfectionist or people who have high standards of our work. There is always room to improve and it feels like an endless goal striving for satisfaction. 

I like how they talked about ""talent"" and how it is used. I get that a lot and sometimes it is nice to hear, but sometimes it does undermine how much work you had to do to get to where you are. It is especially discouraging when you are in an art class in college and complete beginners are surpassing you in understanding perspectives, lighting, and use of colors. 

I wonder how much this resonated with the artists involved with both the Manga and anime? I would really like to see a behind the scene look."
