128705,IV0-SYn3YuM,Ugykuhao-BYHpR4HzBB4AaABAg,2021-09-27T17:05:55Z,667,8,"I first found this manga 2 years ago, when I was on my 2nd semester of art school in graphic design. It was like my whole self was laid bare to me. All of my insecurities are spoken aloud to me face by this manga. Because, just like yatora, I knew nothing about art before deciding to pursue it. Well, I have a bit of head start actually. I've always been drawing anime girls and sold them to get a bit of pocket money, trade them with friends and always watching videos of my favourite mangaka doing their work. And yet I've done nothing to improve myself. I choose to take the course because that's just 'the natural thing to do' since I meddled a bit with it. Heck, I even promised the professors that I would work hard, saying that I can endure it since I've always admired those who've take art, and disgusted by those who doesn't appreciate it. But alas my arrogance brings me nowhere. How helpless I am in an environment where a mere line was enough to tell either you're good or not. I broke down on my second semester and finally drop out on my 3rd semester which coincidentally happened during the pandemic. And I don't draw anything for a year. I hate seeing what I draw. Even the act of picking up a pencil is scary for me. And yet whenever I read this manga, it's like I want to believe that there's still hope. That I don't actually hate drawing. Everytime I read this manga, I feels like my eyes have been opened more and more. I don't have to stick to drawing, I can try to be a translator but I'm still mediocre at languages so.... Anyway, this year managed to create to drawings that make my heart feels like I'm enjoying drawing so much. I don't know what tomorrow will brings to me but I hope just for another day, that I don't hate what I drew."
