128705,IV0-SYn3YuM,Ugwa5RmpLYji5eA3AON4AaABAg,2021-09-25T12:49:39Z,52,2,"Netflix is sure surprising us with their anime licenses lately and on top of that, they manage to beat out Funimation and Crunchyroll on _Blue Period,_ and _Komi Can't Communicate_ for it's Fall lineup. I have a hunch that part of the reason for Netflix licensing and acquiring these two particular shows for their streaming service is also due to the Sony/Funimation acquisition of Crunchyroll and they need some anime titles that will attract users to subscribe to their service along with changing their strategy to release their anime hence why they are now starting to release their anime shows weekly which is what they're doing with Blue Period and Komi.

I'm so excited to see both of those series be dropped weekly on Netflix instead of just holding onto the series before dropping it on the service after its Japanese airing 3-4 months later so no more of the ""Netflix Jail"" complaints, I'm optimistic that Netflix will start releasing anime series they license/acquired weekly on their service."
