103632,UZE4ZZiXBQY,UgyFH7Ueb4xUvKVlf5p4AaABAg,2021-01-01T15:59:38Z,0,0,"gonna be honest, spider isekai is too slow paced for me to be an anime, i don't know when they are going to end for the anime s1(multi season or one shot anime?) but from what i remeber it will be painful because all the good stuff are really late.

if i have to compare this with slime sekai then slime win hand down both in the starting and late developing, i would say that spider isekai have some similarity with slime but is more focus into character develop(skil wise) and information, meanwhile slime is more focuseed in world building and new characters.
as you can guess for mee slime just better in almost every scenario.

another comparison is to attack on titan where from the first season thing is pretty high paced and full of stuff, the common thing is that later on(second+ season) thing get more interesting, but the problem with spider as i said is the slow pace.

a similar anime about the rythm is bookworm, both start slow and focus you into a specific environment in order to let you see the little detail of the wolrd just to break it up into showing you a bigger world later on."
