153800,oh7bd-CDY6U,UgxkZvsg9MPtMyJwfip4AaABAg,2025-10-09T20:00:04Z,1,0,"So, the animation seems improved compared to the second season, but it still doesn’t reach the level of the first. It’s a shame, because a series like One-Punch Man requires very fluid, detailed, and impactful animation to truly do justice to the manga’s artwork. It’s unfortunate that the animation studio changed from Madhouse to J.C.Staff, which hasn’t proven to be on par with its predecessor.
If everything had remained in Madhouse’s hands, it certainly would have been better: in addition to a higher level of animation quality, the general interest in the series might have stayed high, and there probably wouldn’t have been such a long gap between seasons.

I’ll definitely watch this season, because One-Punch Man is one of my favorite manga/anime. I’m just disappointed that there has been such a significant drop in animation quality compared to the first season."
